# The coefficient field of an eigenform is a number field

Theorem statement: `MTT.numberField_coefficientField` (`8c4d2529-1d78-4052-9180-85a6dc276fb0`), by
davidloeffler, 2026-09-20.

Proof: submission `5d72e2d4-d3df-4541-bf3b-ab2eb7bddb57`, by davidloeffler, 2026-09-20 (ACCEPTED);
locally adapted.

Let $f$ be an MTT eigenform of positive level $N$ and weight $k \ge 2$. Its coefficient field $K_f$,
generated over $\mathbb Q$ by all Fourier coefficients and all values of the nebentype, is a number
field:
$$
[K_f : \mathbb Q] < \infty.
$$
This packages finite-dimensionality into Mathlib's standard NumberField predicate, making the
arithmetic of its integer ring and residue fields directly available.

## Explanation of the source proof

For an eigenform $f$, the previously established theorem supplies
$$
\dim_{\mathbb Q} K_f < \infty.
$$
After installing this finite-dimensional vector-space structure, Mathlib's
NumberField.of_module_finite gives the standard NumberField predicate immediately.

<!-- Generated by add_prove2me_provenance.py -->
